# Cumulonimbus VDB baked cloud card

Created an independent RX cloud card in the currently open `/Game/Study/Sky_CloudV3/L_SkyCloudV3_Showcase` level, using selected actor `SCV3_Approved_LowerSoftMassDay` as the material/mesh reference.

## Assets and usage

- Folder: `/Game/RXSkySystem/CloudCards/Cumulonimbus01`.
- Actor: `RX_Cumulonimbus01_BakedCard`, folder `RXSkySystem/CloudCards`.
- Blueprint: `Blueprints/BP_RXCloudCard_Cumulonimbus01`.
- Material: `Materials/M_RXCloudCard`, independently copied from the reference's native three-colour cloud shader.
- Mesh: `Meshes/SM_Cumulonimbus01_DomePatch`, independent copy of the reference curved patch. Component Y scale 0.703155 corrects its wide aspect for the square bake.
- Current texture: `Textures/T_Cumulonimbus01_Beauty45BackRGBA`, 1024×1024, linear HDR RGBA with alpha, mipmaps and clamp addressing. The original grayscale `T_Cumulonimbus01_BeautyRGBA` and earlier `T_Cumulonimbus01_ThreeWayRGBA` remain historical bakes. Original grayscale alpha remains the coverage source.

The BP exposes the reference controls for highlight/midtone/shadow colours, their remap points, contrast, softness, opacity and flip. It creates its own dynamic material in its native construction script. Default `CloudContrast=1.15` and `CloudMidBias=0` soften the VDB lighting relative to the source actor's 2 / 0.45. The other palette values were copied from the selected actor. This is a fixed-view baked card, not a new live volume or replacement for the main RX sky dome.

## Bake

Source: `/Game/RXSkySystem/VDB/VDB_Texture_Collection/Volume_01/VDB_AP_Cumulonimbus_Cloud/AP_Cumulonimbus_Cloud_01`, grid 343×347×384.

Used a temporary Cloud Forge heterogeneous-volume actor with native frame transform, scale 50 and density multiplier 1. A temporary directional light used intensity 8, pitch -35°, yaw 35°. A fixed perspective SceneCapture2D at the volume centre minus 35000 on Y looked along +Y at 25° FOV. Fog, atmosphere and sky contributions were excluded from the capture. A 512-pixel probe preceded the final 1024-pixel capture to limit GPU load. This was not a temporal accumulation or an upscale.

Scene-colour HDR plus inverse opacity was converted to straight grayscale RGB and coverage: `alpha=1-capture.a`, `shade=sqrt(saturate(luminance(capture.rgb)/max(alpha,.001)*1.6))`. The reference shader uses this luminance to interpolate its three palette colours. Raw source is retained as `Baking/T_Cumulonimbus01_Raw`; the packing material is `/Game/RXSkySystem/Baking/CloudCards/Cumulonimbus01/M_PackBeauty`.

## Validation and preservation

- Material and BP compile with zero errors; BP has zero warnings.
- Source-art alpha includes fully transparent and fully opaque pixels. Sampled dark interior pixels remain opaque.
- Final BP dependency closure contains the owned RX card assets, shared sky collection (added below), and native NavigationSystem. No Study, VDB, SkyDomeTools or MCP dependency is required by the finished card.
- Original selected actor/material were left intact. Three original cloud actors were briefly hidden for an isolated screenshot, then restored.
- Temporary source/capture/light actors were removed; current level was saved and the new card selected.
- Screenshots and inspection evidence: `MCPGameProject/Saved/RXSelectedCloudStudy/`. Existing scene fog/palette still influence its final appearance; a baked view cannot supply true volume parallax.

## Sun occlusion and sky-colour fill

The copied material's opacity component mask had R, G and A enabled. Its scalar opacity therefore used the first colour component instead of coverage alpha. Dark areas revealed both the sky and the solar disc. Corrected this mask to A only in the owned RX material; the original reference cloud material is unchanged.

To preserve the user's preferred sky-colour blending, coverage now controls occlusion separately from cloud shading. The material reconstructs the current sky gradient, haze, procedural wisps and broad halo, excluding the solar disc. This background fills dark cloud regions while dense coverage blocks the disc. Feathered edges remain soft. No VDB rebake or higher-resolution render target was required.

`/Game/RXSkySystem/CloudCards/Shared/MPC_CloudCardSky` carries the sky parameters. The current Study sky BP writes these with native collection setters in its construction script. The card contains a local copy of the sky shading expressions and reads the shared collection, so it has no asset dependency on the Study shader. In another sky system, its controller must supply matching collection values; saved defaults match this scene. One active sky provider per world is assumed. Runtime changes that bypass this construction script must also update the collection.

Both `RX_Cumulonimbus01_BakedCard` instances use the fixed material. User transforms and palette values were retained. The same-camera screenshot shows the sun blocked behind the upper card with surrounding sky colours retained. BP compile: zero errors/warnings; material compile: zero errors. A temporary SkyContrast change confirmed native collection propagation, then the exact original value was restored. Asset-registry dependency audit found no MCP references. Current showcase level saved. Evidence: `MCPGameProject/Saved/RXCloudCardSun/after_complete.png` and `final_validation.json`.

## Three-direction lighting upgrade

Applied to the remaining user-edited `RX_Cumulonimbus01_BakedCard2` in the current showcase. Its transform, scale and existing palette controls were preserved. The BP and material defaults now use `T_Cumulonimbus01_ThreeWayRGBA`.

| Channel | Data |
| --- | --- |
| R | VDB illuminated from +Z (top) |
| G | VDB illuminated from -Z (bottom) |
| B | VDB illuminated from the fixed bake camera side (-Y/front) |
| A | Original BeautyRGBA coverage, copied without lighting modification |

Three sequential 1024-square SceneColorHDR captures used the original VDB/frame, density 1, scale 50, 25-degree camera along +Y, and white directional light intensity 8. Volume centre and extents exactly match the original bake. Atmosphere, sky lighting and fog are excluded. Each RGB basis is linear unpremultiplied luminance divided by light intensity 8; no per-direction normalization or baked colour tint. Raw captures remain in `Baking/T_ThreeWayRaw_Top`, `Bottom` and `Front`. Packing material is `/Game/RXSkySystem/Baking/CloudCards/Cumulonimbus01/M_PackThreeWay`. Temporary capture, volume and light actors were removed.

The material sums each basis times its independent colour/strength. `sqrt(saturate(luminance * LightResponseGain))` feeds the existing palette ramp; normalized directional colour tints that palette. The existing sky-fill and alpha holdout remain in place. Controls under **Directional Lighting** are instance editable, use English names, and have Korean tooltips:

| Parameter | Default |
| --- | --- |
| TopLightStrength | 1.0 |
| BottomLightStrength | 0.08 |
| FrontLightStrength | 0.25 |
| LightResponseGain | 12.8 |
| TopLightColor / BottomLightColor / FrontLightColor | White |

These were initially manual weights in the baked card's local frame. The directional-light integration below supersedes that behavior by default. Independent left/right and backlighting were not baked. This remains a fixed-view 2D card. No new C++ or runtime authoring dependency was introduced.

Verified all seven BP controls are instance editable and propagate into the card MID. BP/material compilation passes with no errors, and the BP has no warnings. A defaults recompile retained the new texture and white colour defaults. Top-only and bottom-only screenshots visibly illuminate different parts of the cloud; the final actor values were restored afterward. Packed alpha spans 0–1; RGB channels differ (top/bottom correlation approximately -0.028). Source and review images preserve their intended alpha: packed coverage remains meaningful, screenshot alpha is uniformly 255. Native dependency audit found no MCP references. Current level saved; other dirty packages were not saved. Evidence is in `MCPGameProject/Saved/RXCloudCardThreeWay/`.

Authoring scripts: `scripts/bake_rx_cloud_card_three_way_ue.py` (explicit setup/aim/capture/pack/cleanup phases) and `scripts/apply_rx_cloud_card_three_way_ue.py` (one-shot reviewed material/BP integration with checkpoint). Inspect existing output/state before reuse; these deliberately refuse blind replay.

## Live directional-light response

The current `DirectionalLight` has **Atmosphere Sun Light** enabled at index **0**. The material now reads native `SkyAtmosphereLightDirection(0)` and transforms its world direction into card-local coordinates. UE 5.6 supplies this uniform even without a SkyAtmosphere component (confirmed in the installed engine's SceneRendering.cpp). This updates in the editor and game without Python, BP tick, or reconstructing the cloud when the light rotates.

The direction points toward the light. Weights are `max(localZ,0)` for top, `max(-localZ,0)` for bottom, and `max(-localX,0)` for front; the card's inward-facing front is local -X. Existing direction strengths become art multipliers. Untouched old defaults of Bottom 0.08 / Front 0.25 were changed to 1 / 1 so those light directions can actually illuminate their basis; other user overrides were retained.

- `DirectionalLightInfluence=1`: fully automatic direction weights. Set 0 for the previous manual sum.
- `AmbientFillStrength=0.15`: weak front-basis fill, independent of light direction, to retain some form where the three-direction basis is incomplete.
- Both controls are instance editable under Directional Lighting, with English names and Korean tooltips.

Verified opposite light rotations change the rendered top/bottom shading without running the cloud construction script. The user's original light rotation was restored (pitch 37, yaw -106, roll -171), and the current level was saved. BP/material compile passes; dependency audit contains no MCP references. Evidence: `MCPGameProject/Saved/RXCloudCardDirectionalLight/`. Implementation: `scripts/connect_rx_cloud_card_directional_light_ue.py`.

Only direction is connected here; light colour/intensity remain the card's artistic controls. The procedural sky-disc direction remains controlled by its existing sky BP. Use the designated atmosphere light at index 0; arbitrary additional directional lights are not summed. Side/back illumination has no dedicated bake, so this is a three-basis approximation, not six-way relighting.

## Current basis: beauty 45 degrees and backlight (2026-09-18)

The user replaced the vertical top/bottom/front proposal with **R=front upper45, G=front lower45, B=backlight, A=coverage**. This section supersedes the earlier channel layout and direction-weight calculations above.

Rebaked the same VDB, bounds, camera and intensity sequentially at 1024 square. Light travel rotations in the bake scene are upper45 `(pitch=-45,yaw=90)`, lower45 `(pitch=45,yaw=90)`, and back `(pitch=0,yaw=-90)`. Existing scene-light visibility was recorded, disabled only during capture, then restored. Scene-light transforms were not altered by baking. Source alpha was copied: exhaustive comparison of the 1,048,576 packed alpha samples against the earlier packed texture gives **maximum difference 0**. New raw captures are `Baking/T_Beauty45Raw_Upper45`, `Lower45` and `Back`; packing material is `/Game/RXSkySystem/Baking/CloudCards/Cumulonimbus01/M_PackBeauty45`.

The material still reads native atmosphere light 0 in card-local space. It now interpolates the three sampled directions around the front/up plane using smooth angular segments. Front light blends upper/lower; each captured direction selects its own basis; the back-angle wrap is continuous. Automatic direction weights sum to 1, with ambient fill added separately. Near pure side light the weights blend to the upper/lower average because no side basis was baked. Thus this is deliberately an artistic approximation between three measurements, not full spherical relighting.

Controls:

- Existing `TopLightStrength/Color` now control front-upper45 and `BottomLightStrength/Color` front-lower45; English Upper/Lower 45 display metadata and Korean tooltips describe the new directions.
- New instance-editable `BackLightStrength=1` and `BackLightColor=white` replace the former Front controls. Existing actor Front values were migrated to Back; old BP fields remain non-instance-editable legacy values, and unused Front material parameter expressions were removed.
- `BackCoreContrast=0.25` reduces the sky-colour fill in covered, dim core regions only while backlit. Coverage and sun occlusion remain unchanged. Set 0 to disable this artistic core contrast.
- `AmbientFillStrength` now uses the mean of upper/lower beauty channels rather than a front-only channel.

User-updated cloud position/scale and palette were preserved. In-editor tests with actual directional-light rotations show distinct upper45, lower45 and backlighting without reconstructing the card. Full backlighting now retains a shaded core and the baked illuminated rim. The light's original rotation (pitch 60, yaw -140, roll -109) was restored after these tests. Current showcase map saved; unrelated dirty assets left untouched. Material/BP compilation and native-only dependency audit pass. Evidence and opaque review PNGs: `MCPGameProject/Saved/RXCloudCardBeauty45/`.

Authoring: `scripts/bake_rx_cloud_card_beauty45_ue.py` and `scripts/apply_rx_cloud_card_beauty45_ue.py`. The same fixed-view and independent sky-disc limitations still apply.

## RX sky palette integration (2026-09-18)

The user placed two cards in `/Game/RXSkySystem/Cubeless/Maps/L_RXSkySystem_Cubeless`. Their previous Study sky fill and daytime palette did not follow the RX twilight sky. The cards now consume the RX system's evaluated environment through `/Game/RXSkySystem/CloudCards/Shared/MPC_RXCloudCardEnvironment`.

`BP_RXSkySystem_Cubeless.UpdateSky` ends with native `SyncCloudCardEnvironment`. It reads 17 scalar and nine vector parameters from `TODCloudMID`, then publishes them and `Active=1` into the collection. This shares the actual interpolated sky colours, sun direction, light colour/intensity, ambient colour/intensity, moonlight strength and global tint/intensity. Material-instance getters are impure in UE 5.6: each getter is explicitly executed before its collection setter. No Python or authoring plugin is required during playback.

`M_RXCloudCard` reconstructs the same RX sky gradient and broad aerial tint without celestial discs. Direct lighting uses the existing three baked bases; environment fill and an artistic moon fill keep the cloud readable at night. RX colour evaluation replaces the old independent card palette while this collection is active. `CloudColorIntensity` still provides a local brightness multiplier. The RX global tint/intensity is applied once. Source texture, alpha coverage, holdout and actor transforms were not edited. The collection defaults to inactive, preserving the previous Study-world shading when no RX sky publishes an environment. This global collection assumes one active RX sky per world.

For review, select `RXSkySystem` and change `TimeOfDay`; card reconstruction is unnecessary. Day 12.0, sunset 17.8 and night 22.0 were reviewed in the editor. The original time 19.7760009765625 was restored and the current map saved. RX BP compiles with zero warnings/errors and the material compiles without errors. Dependency inspection found only native engine/project content references, with no MCP references. The full offline verification profile passed. Unrelated dirty material and probe packages were not saved.

Evidence: `MCPGameProject/Saved/RXCloudCardSkyIntegration/` (`day.png`, `sunset.png`, `night.png`, `final.png`, `final_audit.json`, `full_verification.log`). Authoring script: `scripts/integrate_rx_cloud_card_environment_ue.py`, explicit setup/material phases with pre-edit backups; inspect partial state before rerunning.

