Cleaned `M_RXCloudCard` from 107 to 93 expressions. Removed 21 Custom inputs absent from the corresponding HLSL, their now-unreferenced collection expressions, and two duplicate world-space camera-vector expressions. Removed the unused Study solar-disc local calculation and obsolete top/bottom/front channel comment. Retained the Study fallback, RX environment integration, native directional-light response, palette controls, coverage and celestial holdout. Named the Custom nodes by purpose and automatically arranged the graph. No Blueprint, collection asset, texture or level edits were needed.

All retained input links were compared against the original graph, allowing only the equivalent camera-vector substitution; material output connections are identical. Material compilation finished with zero errors and dependency audit contains no MCP references. The immediate post-compile screenshot briefly omitted the card while its dynamic instance shader updated; after instance compilation, the card renders normally. The live background moves between captures, so the raw screenshots are not a pixel-identical regression test. Evidence and the pre-edit backup are under `MCPGameProject/Saved/RXCloudCardCleanup/`; authoring script is `scripts/cleanup_rx_cloud_card_material_ue.py`.

## Alpha-composite colour weight correction

RX integration previously filled all coverage with cloud colour, weakening the earlier shade-to-sky compositing appearance. The RX branch now uses `coverage * lerp(0.25, 1, smoothstep(0.08, 0.90, rxShape))` as its colour weight; `rxShape` blends the existing contrast-shaped directional response toward ambient form at night. The complementary weight fills with the evaluated RX sky colour. Output holdout alpha is unchanged, keeping celestial occlusion independent of shade colour mixing. The shader remains AlphaComposite with premultiplied colour.

The material compiled and saved successfully. A 10,201-case numerical check confirms nonnegative colour weights bounded by holdout and zero contribution at zero coverage; the full offline profile passed. During subsequent instance-statistics inspection the editor exited with D3D12 viewport error `80070005`. After restarting, the saved shader marker was read back successfully, but the editor remained at `/Temp/Untitled_0` behind the `이에타 상태` startup window. Native deferred opening of the RX preview map is queued; post-change visual review is still pending. Do not interpret the numerical/offline checks as a visual pass. Evidence: `MCPGameProject/Saved/RXCloudCardAlphaBlend/`; implementation: `scripts/fix_rx_cloud_card_alpha_blend_ue.py`.

Follow-up: the Restore Packages modal was subsequently cleared and the RX preview map opened. Verified the saved correction is present and visually reviewed daytime, sunset 17.8 and night 22.0. Sunset initially lost too much interior form, so `rxShape` now uses `lerp(max(form, ambientForm * 0.70), ambientForm, night)`. This retains baked internal detail in backlighting while preserving shade-to-sky mixing. Output alpha/holdout remains unchanged. Final sunset and current-time captures are `sunset_final.png` and `final.png`. Restored the user's current time 10.944000244140625 and left the editor on this map. The final material compiled and saved with zero errors; the full offline profile was rerun for this shader adjustment.

## RX cloud shader on the plane/card — six-direction variant

Applied `/Game/RXSkySystem/CloudCards/Cumulonimbus01/Materials/M_RXCloudCard_SixWay` to the two existing placed cards by changing their `CloudMaterialTemplate` overrides. Preserved the previous material and textures for comparison. The Blueprint's default template is still the previous variant; duplicate an updated placed card to retain the six-direction setup, or assign the new template explicitly.

The new material copies the current `M_Cubeless_Clouds_Fog` shader, including its transport interpolation, phase/scattering, ambient and multiple-scattering terms, painterly sky integration, twilight/night grading, curve atlas and AlphaComposite celestial holdout. Replaced panorama projection/advection with the card's mesh UV and optional FlipX. Directional transport is evaluated in the card's local frame; solar elevation for palette grading and the phase angle remain world-space. Dome horizon clipping is disabled for independently placed cards. Forty unused copied expressions were removed (59 expressions remain).

Two linear HDR 1024-square textures hold the RX transport layout:

| Texture | R | G | B | A |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `T_Cumulonimbus01_RXPositive` | Local +X at elevation 20° | Local +Y at elevation 20° | +Z/top | Original coverage |
| `T_Cumulonimbus01_RXNegative` | Local -X at elevation 20° | Local -Y at elevation 20° | -Z/bottom | Mean of four horizontal captures |

Captured the four elevated ring directions and four horizontal directions sequentially from the same VDB/camera. Reused the existing matching top/bottom raw captures. Raw RGB stores premultiplied luminance per unit white-light intensity, not the earlier unpremultiplied beauty basis. Coverage was copied from the original BeautyRGBA. Canvas packing targets must be cleared to alpha 1 because the packing helper writes inverse opacity; the initial alpha-zero pack was corrected before final validation/application. Scene lights were restored and temporary capture actors removed. No project C++ was changed.

Existing `LightResponseGain=12.8` maps to transport calibration 4 (`gain * 0.3125`) for the HV-to-RX bake response range; sharp and broad mip samples receive the same calibration. Card opacity, alpha power, FlipX and colour intensity remain connected. The RX environment collection drives time-dependent sky palette, sun direction, light/ambient intensity and global colour. Other RX shader art controls were copied from the current evaluated CloudDome MID at setup; they are defaults of the new material, not newly synchronized BP controls. Old beauty-direction/palette controls do not drive this variant.

Reviewed day 12, sunset 17.8 and night 22 in the editor. Restored the user's time 12.86400032043457 and saved the current RX preview map with both assignments. Material compilation passes and the new material/textures have no MCP dependencies. Source old material remains available for comparison. Evidence: `MCPGameProject/Saved/RXCloudCardSixWay/`; scripts: `bake_rx_cloud_card_sixway_ue.py` and `apply_rx_cloud_card_sixway_ue.py`.
